"YOUR PLAN" v. "REALITY" 

FUNDAMENTALS
Simple straight-line "YOUR PLAN" bike ride to a finish flag with
the complex, obstacle-filled "REALITY" of hills, water, ladders,
and detours.

A straight-line plan has vanishing geodesic curvature:
kappa_g = 0

A general plane curve r(s) has geodesic curvature
kappa_g(s) = | r'(s) x r''(s) | / | r'(s) |^3

The extra "effort" of reality is the integral of |kappa_g(s)| ds
along the actual path.

EQUATIONS

YOUR PLAN (idealized)

y_plan(x) = 0

or parametrically

r_plan(t) = ( t , 0 )          t in [0, L]

REALITY (simple analytic model)

y_real(x) = A * sin(k1 * x)
          B * sin(k2 * x)
          C * exp( -(x - x0)^2 / sigma^2 )

(plus optional piecewise jumps for cliffs, water, tunnels)

NOTATION AND TYPES

x          : horizontal coordinate          (real scalar)
t          : path parameter                 (real scalar)
L          : total planned length           (positive real)
y(x)       : height function                (real-valued function of x)
r(t)       : position vector                (R^2-valued function of t)
A, B, C    : amplitude coefficients         (real scalars)
k1, k2     : spatial frequencies            (real scalars)
x0         : obstacle center                (real scalar)
sigma      : obstacle width                 (positive real)
kappa_g    : geodesic curvature             (real-valued function of arc-length s)
